+# October 2026 development diary
+
+## 2026-10-15 — Clean SM-S908U1 Android build lane
+
+Created a standalone `android-s22u` product branch for Ali's US-unlocked Samsung
+Galaxy S22 Ultra (`SM-S908U1`, Snapdragon/Adreno). It uses the distinct
+`io.github.alibahaa01.generalszh` application ID, so community APKs that used
+`me.generalsx.zh` cannot cause a signature conflict with this build.
+
+The Android workflow had drifted back to the experimental DXVK 2.6 source even
+though the maintenance handover states that shipped mobile builds use DXVK
+Native 1.9.2b plus d3d8to9. The workflow now fetches exact reviewed commits,
+applies the repository's Android/arm64 patches, builds only D3D9, builds the
+64-bit-safe d3d8to9 frontend separately, and rejects artifacts that do not
+identify as DXVK 1.9.2 or AArch64. The installable artifact is a debug-signed
+arm64 APK; a release APK is also assembled but remains unsigned.
+
+The reported device log stopped while `StdBIGFileSystem` was initializing. The
+launcher file check previously read only a BIG archive's 16-byte header, while
+the native parser trusted entry counts, offsets, sizes, and unbounded path
+strings. Both layers now validate the complete directory table. Play performs
+the check automatically, verifies the engine-specific startup archive
+(`INIZH.big` or `INI.big`), and blocks native startup with a readable report if
+the imported data is incomplete. The native reader independently bounds every
+read and records the rejected archive in exported stderr rather than overrunning
+its path buffer. JVM tests cover valid, truncated, out-of-range, unterminated,
+and overlong BIG directory entries.
+
+Build and real-device validation are still required. The acceptance run is:
+install beside the old package, import the complete Steam Zero Hour directory,
+launch on the SM-S908U1, enter a skirmish, and export the engine log if startup
+does not reach the menu.
-- 
